{%- comment -%}
  horizon-blocks Phase 2 — `_heading` private text primitive.

  Verbatim port of stock Horizon v4.1.1 (68760d9) blocks/_heading.liquid with
  t: strings hardcoded to English (from Horizon's en.default.schema.json).
  Deviations — the same two the Phase-1b text block carries:

  - The custom-preset Font select is trimmed 4 -> 2 options (Body/Heading):
    under the adapt mapping Dawn has 2 real font settings, so Horizon's 4 role
    labels would offer the design team duplicate choices. All four
    --font-{role}--* token sets remain defined in hz-type-variables, so
    hand-written JSON using subheading/accent values still resolves.
  - The type_preset `info` key is dropped — Horizon's links to per-preset
    theme settings that don't exist in Dawn (presets are hardcoded at stock
    Horizon defaults in snippets/hz-type-variables.liquid).

  The renderer reuses the frozen 1b snippets/text.liquid unchanged — it
  already accepts `fallback_text`, and its px re-emission covers this
  schema's rem font_size values (Dawn rem trap). `text` below is a render
  param only when the block is statically rendered with one (Horizon
  convention); nil on normal insertion, so fallback_text stays blank.
{%- endcomment -%}

{% render 'text', width: '100%', block: block, fallback_text: text %}

